                    },
                    "name": "Company Background LLM"
                  },
                  "outcomes": {
                    "success": "1770217020095"
                  },
                  "code": "PRJ_PJF_LLM_COMPANY_BACKGROUND",
                  "id": "1770216037305",
                  "inputs": [
                    {
                      "id": "1770216037310_1",
                      "name": "prompt",
                      "type": "string",
                      "value": "###References\nCompany Name: {{$context.$variables.prjPjfVarUqPromptParameters.CompanyBackground.company_name}}\nProject Name: {{$context.$variables.prjPjfVarUqPromptParameters.CompanyBackground.project_name}}\nSummary Length: {{$context.$variables.prjPjfVarUqPromptParameters.CompanyBackground.summary_length}}\n\n###Instructions\nCraft a comprehensive overview of {{$context.$variables.prjPjfVarUqPromptParameters.CompanyBackground.company_name}} in a single paragraph for a new project proposal. This overview should encapsulate the company's background, including its history, mission, vision, core values, and industry. Highlight the company's organizational culture and reliability to help potential clients or partners understand its strengths, and showcase the extensive experience and expertise of {{$context.$variables.prjPjfVarUqPromptParameters.CompanyBackground.company_name}} in delivering transformational projects. Conclude by clearly articulating how the company's goals and values align with the project's objectives, demonstrating a strategic fit. Explain convincingly why company is the ideal partner for this project by emphasizing its strong track record, proven expertise, and relevant capabilities. \nUse the company name and project name as is. Do not interpret, narrate, or elaborate on the project name within the company background summary.\nDo not include the count of the workforce. Avoid mentioning the duration of the company's history.\nAim for a narrative that is strictly within {{$context.$variables.prjPjfVarUqPromptParameters.CompanyBackground.summary_length}} words. The summary should leave the reader confident in the company's ability to deliver successful project outcomes.\n\nRespond with the language: {{$context.$nodes.PRJ_PJF_TOOL_GETUSERSESSION.$output.items[0].Language}}\n\n###Acceptance Criteria\n1. Narrative should be in the perspective of {{$context.$variables.prjPjfVarUqPromptParameters.CompanyBackground.company_name}}.\n2. The company background should be seamlessly integrated with the project details, providing a narrative that flows naturally and compellingly.\n3. Ensure the overview is clear, direct, and avoids unnecessary elaboration. Each sentence should serve a specific purpose, contributing to a focused and succinct narrative.\n4. Employ straightforward, professional language, maintain a third-person perspective, and keep the tone neutral.\n5. The proposal should be direct, informative, and compelling, crafted without formal closures or signatures, and avoiding direct quotations or data enumeration.\n6. Ensure that the references blend naturally into the narrative without disrupting the flow or clarity. Revise any awkward phrasing or mismatches in tone or language.\n7. Use the value of the variable {{$context.$variables.prjPjfVarUqPromptParameters.CompanyBackground.project_name}} as it is without any truncation.\n\n###Formatting\n1. The narrative should unfold seamlessly without explicit section headers or introductory phrases that fragment the content.\n2. Avoid any form of listing, such as bullet points or numbered items, to ensure a natural, fluid delivery that embeds the data into the narrative without partitioning the content artificially.\n\n###Final Check\n1. Ensure that the content should be delivered in a single, unbroken paragraph with no additional formatting elements like headers, line breaks, or extra unnecessary special characters like }, ##, or >."
                    }
                  ],
                  "type": "LLM"
                },
                {
                  "metadata": {
                    "modelConfiguration": {
                      "modelProperties": {
                        "k": 0,
                        "max_tokens": 4000,
                        "p": 0.75
                      },
                      "code": "ORA_LLM_MODEL_PROVIDER_CERT_BASIC_LLAMA_3_3_70B",
                      "model": "ORA_LLM_MODEL_GPT_OSS_120B",
                      "modelName": "GPT-OSS-120B",
                      "provider": "CERT_BASIC"
                    },
                    "name": "Executive Summary LLM"
                  },
                  "outcomes": {
                    "success": "1770217242748"
                  },
                  "code": "PRJ_PJF_LLM_EXECUTIVE_SUMMARY",
                  "id": "1770216074626",
                  "inputs": [
                    {
                      "id": "1770216074627_1",
                      "name": "prompt",
                      "type": "string",
                      "value": "###References\nProposing Company: {{$context.$variables.prjPjfVarUqPromptParameters.ExecutiveSummary.proposing_company}}\nClient Company: {{$context.$variables.prjPjfVarUqPromptParameters.ExecutiveSummary.client_company}}\nProject Details: {{$context.$variables.prjPjfVarUqPromptParameters.ExecutiveSummary.project_details}}\nProject: {{$context.$variables.prjPjfVarUqPromptParameters.ExecutiveSummary.project_name}}\nSummary Length: {{$context.$variables.prjPjfVarUqPromptParameters.ExecutiveSummary.summary_length}}\n\nYou are an experienced Project Manager at the Proposing Company with a strong track record in delivering successful projects. Your task is to write a one-paragraph executive summary that's about 150 words for the Project. This summary should be concise and capture the key elements of the project based on the provided project details . The summary is intended for a proposal to the client company.\n\nBegin with a brief description of the project, including its name, scope, and key deliverables. Clearly articulate the problem or challenge that the project aims to address. If no specific problem is identified in the project details, outline the opportunity or strategic objective that the project aims to achieve. Avoid refrencing the project details as a challenge when no challenge is explicitly mentioned. Maintain accuracy and alignment with the provided information.\n\nThen, list the main goals of the project and the key objectives that will measure its success. Explain how these objectives align with the broader organizational goals. Highlight why this project is critical for the organization, including the expected benefits, and how it will address stakeholder needs or improve business operations. Emphasize the importance of collaboration between all stakeholders, and how the shared commitment between the client company and proposing company will drive the project's success.\n\nWrap up with a confident statement that reinforces the project's potential for success and its alignment with the organization's strategic priorities.\n\nEnsure this single paragraph summary is concise, accurate, and compelling to capture the reader's attention in exactly one paragraph while avoiding any speculative information. Avoid repeating key details.\n\nAim for a narrative that is strictly one paragraph and within the summary length in terms of the number of words. \n\nRespond with the language: {{$context.$nodes.PRJ_PJF_TOOL_GETUSERSESSION.$output.items[0].Language}}\n\n### Acceptance Criteria\n1. The executive summary should employ straightforward, professional language, maintain a third-person perspective, and keep the tone neutral.\n2. Use the value of the variable {{$context.$variables.prjPjfVarUqPromptParameters.ExecutiveSummary.project_name}} as it is without any truncation.\n3. The proposal should be direct, informative, and crafted without formal closures or signatures and avoiding direct quotations or data enumeration.\n4. Ensure the narrative is concise and avoids redundant details or over-elaboration, with each sentence serving a specific purpose.\n5. Integrate the project name and project details seamlessly into the narrative, ensuring a coherent and compelling flow.\n6. Ensure the overview is clear, direct, and avoids unnecessary elaboration. Each sentence should serve a specific purpose, contributing to a focused and succinct narrative.\n\n### Formatting\n1. The narrative should unfold seamlessly, integrating insights directly without explicit section headers or introductory phrases that fragment the content. \n2. Avoid any form of listing, such as bullet points or numbered items, to ensure a natural fluid delivery that embeds the data into the narrative without partitioning the content artificially.\n\n###Final Check\n1. Ensure that the response is a single paragraph with no additional formatting elements like headers, line breaks, new lines, ##, or any other unnecessary special characters.\n2. Ensure the narrative is concise and avoids redundant details or over-elaboration, with each sentence serving a specific purpose.\n3. Do not use the word \"challenges\" unless explicity given one in the input."
                    }
                  ],
                  "type": "LLM"
                },
                {
                  "metadata": {
                    "modelConfiguration": {
                      "modelProperties": {
                        "k": 0,
                        "max_tokens": 4000,
                        "p": 0.75
                      },
                      "code": "ORA_LLM_MODEL_PROVIDER_CERT_BASIC_LLAMA_3_3_70B",
                      "model": "ORA_LLM_MODEL_GPT_OSS_120B",
                      "modelName": "GPT-OSS-120B",
                      "provider": "CERT_BASIC"
                    },
                    "name": "Implementation Plan LLM"
                  },
                  "outcomes": {
                    "success": "1770217294656"
                  },
                  "code": "PRJ_PJF_LLM_IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN",
                  "id": "1770216129491",
                  "inputs": [
                    {
                      "id": "1770216129493_1",
                      "name": "prompt",
                      "type": "string",
                      "value": "### References\nThe name of the project: {{$context.$variables.prjPjfVarUqPromptParameters.ImplementationPlan.project_name}}\nThe project start date: {{$context.$variables.prjPjfVarUqPromptParameters.ImplementationPlan.start_date}}\nThe project finish date: {{$context.$variables.prjPjfVarUqPromptParameters.ImplementationPlan.finish_date}}\nThe overall project duration: {{$context.$variables.prjPjfVarUqPromptParameters.ImplementationPlan.duration}}\nThe estimated project budget: {{$context.$variables.prjPjfVarUqPromptParameters.ImplementationPlan.estimated_budget}}\nThe project plan information: {{$context.$variables.prjPjfVarUqPromptParameters.ImplementationPlan.project_plan_information}}\n\nYou are an experienced Project Manager with expertise in creating detailed implementation plans. Your task is to read and analyze the provided project information to generate a concise, accurate implementation summary in a 3-paragraph format for a client-facing project proposal. The summary should be based entirely on the provided details, with no fabricated information.\n\n### Instructions:\nIntroduction: Begin with an overview of the project name, start date, finish date, duration, and estimated budget (only if the input is not N/A or blank). Use the data from the references specifically the project name, start date, finish date, duration, and estimated budget. Do not provide an overview of the project plan information or any task finish dates in this section. Remember to only mention the budget if it is present in the input.\n\nImplementation Summary: In the next paragraph, summarize the project's implementation plan, based on the project plan information without interpreting new details or explaining what any task is meant to achieve. Cover key tasks and finish date milestones that ensure the project's success. Focus on critical aspects of the project timeline and phases of execution, keeping the summary clear and concise. Make sure to use the precise task names from the input and only refer to these dates in the context of task finish dates. If the project plan information doesn't contains any tasks or milestones, provide a generic response and do not hallucinate any details or talk about the phases, plan, tasks or milestones.\n\nConclusion: Conclude with 2-3 sentences highlighting strategies for progress monitoring, risk management, and quality assurance. Explain how these strategies will ensure the project stays on schedule and within budget, without mentioning specific roles, teams, or individuals. It should be written in a clear, third-person narrative, emphasizing the seamless execution of the project, expected outcomes, and how these align with project goals.\n\nYour summary should be strictly written in a 3-paragraph format and should be at least {{$context.$variables.prjPjfVarUqPromptParameters.ImplementationPlan.summary_length}} words long, offering detailed, informative analysis without unnecessary embellishments. Ensure clarity, professionalism, and use of a third-person perspective. Avoid lists and separate section headers including ones that start with ##.\n\nRespond with the language: {{$context.$nodes.PRJ_PJF_TOOL_GETUSERSESSION.$output.items[0].Language}}\n\n### Acceptance Criteria:\n1. The summary must carefully follow the given structure:\nFirst paragraph: Overview of the project name, start date, finish date, duration, and estimated budget based on the provided in the references.\nSecond paragraph: A concise summary of the project plan information, covering critical aspects of the project timeline's task finish dates.\nThird paragraph: An overview of strategies for monitoring progress, ensuring quality, and managing risks to maintain the schedule and budget.\n2. The length should be at least {{$context.$variables.prjPjfVarUqPromptParameters.ImplementationPlan.summary_length}} words and provide a thorough, detailed summary.\n3. Use clear, professional language, maintain a neutral tone, and ensure third-person narration.\n4. Avoid adding new information, fabricated details, or formal closings and signatures.\n\n### Formatting:\n1. Maintain a seamless narrative flow, integrating project details smoothly without the use of lists, headers, or introductory phrases.\n2. Ensure the narrative reads as a cohesive analysis, embedding project data naturally without artificially partitioning the content.\n3. Do not change the estimated project budget value, making sure to directly copy the currency code and exact usage of commas, spaces, and currency symbols from the references. For example do not change values like \"20,000 EUR\", \"200000 USD\", or \"9,00,000 INR\". When budget is N/A or blank do not include details about the project's budget.\n4. Make sure all dates in the response are formatted like Month Day-Ordinal, Year. For example, February 3rd, 2025. It uses the full month name, the day with an ordinal suffix (e.g., 3rd), and the four-digit year.\n5. Do not add single or double quotation marks around project or task names.\n\n### Final Check\n1. Make sure that the estimated project budget value appears in the summary the exact same way as it does in the references, making sure to remove any currency symbols like dollar signs, if applicable. Otherwise the response will be a failure.\n2. Review the summary for seamless paragraph transitions without any explicit headings. If any labels like \"Introduction,\" \"Implementation Summary,\" or \"Conclusion\" appear, rewrite to ensure smooth integration of content into a narrative format.\n3. Exclude any paragraph headers/sub-headers including ones that use special characters like ##."
                    }
                  ],
                  "type": "LLM"
                },
                {
                  "metadata": {
                    "modelConfiguration": {
                      "modelProperties": {
                        "k": 0,
                        "max_tokens": 4000,
                        "p": 0.75
                      },
                      "code": "ORA_LLM_MODEL_PROVIDER_CERT_BASIC_LLAMA_3_3_70B",
                      "model": "ORA_LLM_MODEL_GPT_OSS_120B",
                      "modelName": "GPT-OSS-120B",
                      "provider": "CERT_BASIC"
                    },
                    "name": "Resource Plan LLM"
                  },
                  "outcomes": {
                    "success": "1770217360405"
                  },
                  "code": "PRJ_PJF_LLM_RESOURCE_PLAN",
                  "id": "1770216161618",
                  "inputs": [
                    {
                      "id": "1770216161621_1",
                      "name": "prompt",
                      "type": "string",
                      "value": "Return ONLY an RFC8259-compliant JSON object with EXACTLY these keys:\nhuman_resource, financial_resource, physical_resource\n\nAlways include all three keys. Each value must be a JSON string.\nDo not output any other keys or any commentary.\n\nMISSING RULE (apply independently per field):\nA field is \"missing\" if, after trimming whitespace, it is \"\" OR equals \"NA\" OR equals \"N/A\" (case-insensitive).\nIf missing -> output \"\" for that key.\nIf not missing -> output a ~80 word paragraph for that key.\n\nDATA (literal inputs; may be empty strings):\n{\n  \"project_name\": \"{{$context.$variables.prjPjfVarUqPromptParameters.ResourcePlan.project_name}}\",\n  \"project_roles\": \"{{$context.$variables.prjPjfVarUqPromptParameters.ResourcePlan.project_roles}}\",\n  \"financial_resources\": \"{{$context.$variables.prjPjfVarUqPromptParameters.ResourcePlan.financial_resources}}\",\n  \"physical_resources\": \"{{$context.$variables.prjPjfVarUqPromptParameters.ResourcePlan.physical_resources}}\"\n}\n\nCONTENT RULES:\n- human_resource: use project_roles. Mention project_name ONLY here.\n  Mention role names; do not explain responsibilities except you may describe 'Project Manager' as competent/adept.\n- financial_resource: use financial_resources. Do NOT mention project_name; say 'the project'.\n  Refer to each listed resource in single quotes (').\n  Avoid specific budget figures.\n- physical_resource: use physical_resources. Do NOT mention project_name; say 'the project'.\n  Refer to each listed resource in single quotes (').\n  Describe condition/functions at a high level; no bullets/lists.\n\nSTYLE:\nThird-person, professional, neutral. No bullets or numbered lists.\n\nOutput only the JSON."
                    }
                  ],
                  "type": "LLM"
                },
